      "text": "## Encapsulation: The Onion of Headers"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#014",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:networking:00-overview, git-history:networking:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "networking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[networking, osi model, tcp/ip, encapsulation, layering]",
        "current_path": "networking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:networking:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "networking",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[networking]",
        "section": "networking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Networking - The Layered Model End-to-End",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Every layer prepends (and sometimes appends) its own header. By the time your\nHTTP request hits the wire it is wrapped four deep. This nesting is called\n**encapsulation**; the unwrapping on the far side is **decapsulation**."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#015",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:networking:00-overview, git-history:networking:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "networking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[networking, osi model, tcp/ip, encapsulation, layering]",
        "current_path": "networking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:networking:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "networking",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[networking]",
        "section": "networking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Networking - The Layered Model End-to-End",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n   APPLICATION:  [ HTTP request bytes ............................. ]\n                                  |\n   TRANSPORT:    [ TCP hdr | HTTP request bytes ................... ]   \"segment\"\n                                  |\n   NETWORK:      [ IP hdr | TCP hdr | HTTP request bytes ......... ]    \"packet\"\n                                  |\n   LINK:         [ ETH hdr | IP hdr | TCP hdr | HTTP bytes | FCS ]      \"frame\"\n                                  |\n   PHYSICAL:     1010110100101110101011010010111010101101001011101...  \"bits\"\n```"
    },
