        "title": "Networking - The Layered Model End-to-End",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A useful discipline: when something breaks, **name the layer**. \"Can't reach the\nhost\" (L3 routing? L2 ARP?) is a different bug from \"connection refused\" (L4 — no\nlistener on the port) which is different from \"TLS handshake failed\" (L6/7 trust)."
    },
