      "text": "## What Each Layer Actually Owns"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#021",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:networking:00-overview, git-history:networking:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "networking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[networking, osi model, tcp/ip, encapsulation, layering]",
        "current_path": "networking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:networking:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "networking",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[networking]",
        "section": "networking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Networking - The Layered Model End-to-End",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The hardest part of networking is keeping straight *which concern lives where*.\nFive different layers all do something that sounds like \"control flow,\" and\nconflating them is the #1 source of confusion. Here is the clean separation."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#022",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:networking:00-overview, git-history:networking:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "networking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[networking, osi model, tcp/ip, encapsulation, layering]",
        "current_path": "networking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:networking:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "networking",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[networking]",
        "section": "networking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Networking - The Layered Model End-to-End",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| CONCERN              | LAYER | MECHANISM           | \"ANSWERS THE Q...\"  |\n|----------------------|-------|---------------------|---------------------|\n| Which physical port? | L2    | MAC switching       | next hop on this LAN |\n| Which global host?   | L3    | IP routing          | next hop toward dest |\n| Which process?       | L4    | port numbers        | which app on the host|\n| Reliable delivery?   | L4    | TCP seq/ack/retx    | did it arrive intact |\n| Don't overrun PEER?  | L4    | flow control (rwnd) | peer's buffer space  |\n| Don't overrun NET?   | L4    | congestion control  | network's capacity   |\n| What's the IP for X? | L7    | DNS                 | name -> address      |\n| Who am I talking to? | L6/7  | TLS / PKI           | identity + secrecy   |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#023",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:networking:00-overview, git-history:networking:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "networking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[networking, osi model, tcp/ip, encapsulation, layering]",
        "current_path": "networking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:networking:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "networking",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[networking]",
        "section": "networking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Networking - The Layered Model End-to-End",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Two pairs deserve special emphasis because they are constantly confused:"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#024",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:networking:00-overview, git-history:networking:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "networking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[networking, osi model, tcp/ip, encapsulation, layering]",
        "current_path": "networking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:networking:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "networking",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[networking]",
        "section": "networking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Networking - The Layered Model End-to-End",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "- **Routing vs. switching.** A *switch* (L2) moves a frame to the right port on\n  one LAN using MAC addresses; it has no idea the Internet exists. A *router*\n  (L3) moves a packet from one network to another using IP prefixes. Switching\n  is \"find the right door in this building\"; routing is \"find the right building\n  in the city.\" (01 and 02 respectively.)"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#025",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:networking:00-overview, git-history:networking:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "networking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[networking, osi model, tcp/ip, encapsulation, layering]",
        "current_path": "networking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:networking:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "networking",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[networking]",
        "section": "networking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Networking - The Layered Model End-to-End",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "- **Flow control vs. congestion control.** Both throttle the sender, but for\n  different reasons. *Flow control* protects the **receiver** from being\n  overrun (its buffer is full). *Congestion control* protects the **network**\n  in between from being overrun (a link is saturated). TCP does both\n  simultaneously with two separate windows. (Covered in 03 and 04.)"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#026",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:networking:00-overview, git-history:networking:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "networking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[networking, osi model, tcp/ip, encapsulation, layering]",
        "current_path": "networking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:networking:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "networking",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[networking]",
        "section": "networking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Networking - The Layered Model End-to-End",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "> **Bridge — addressing vs. routing.** If you have built a distributed system,\n> you already know this split: a service *name* (DNS) resolves to an *address*\n> (IP), which a *routing fabric* delivers to a *port* where a *process* listens.\n> It is the same indirection chain as service discovery → endpoint → load\n> balancer → pod. Networking just standardized it 40 years earlier."
    },
