        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Networking - The Layered Model End-to-End",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Concrete walkthrough — what happens when your laptop loads `https://example.com`.\nEvery numbered directory in this folder owns one step."
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#030",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:networking:00-overview, git-history:networking:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "networking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[networking, osi model, tcp/ip, encapsulation, layering]",
        "current_path": "networking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:networking:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "networking",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[networking]",
        "section": "networking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Networking - The Layered Model End-to-End",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n  YOU TYPE: https://example.com\n     |\n  (1) DNS RESOLUTION                                          --> see 05-DNS\n      \"example.com\" -> 93.184.x.x   (cached? recurse? anycast root?)\n     |\n  (2) ROUTE LOOKUP                                            --> see 02-IP-ROUTING\n      Is dst on my subnet? No -> send to default gateway.\n     |\n  (3) ARP / LINK                                              --> see 01-LINK-LAYER\n      \"What MAC owns the gateway IP?\" -> build Ethernet frame.\n     |\n  (4) NAT (home/CGNAT)                                        --> see 07-NAT\n      Rewrite private src IP:port -> public IP:port; remember mapping.\n     |\n  (5) TCP / QUIC HANDSHAKE                                    --> see 03-TRANSPORT\n      SYN / SYN-ACK / ACK establishes a connection to port 443.\n     |\n  (6) CONGESTION CONTROL ramps the send rate                  --> see 04-CONGESTION\n      slow start -> probe for bandwidth (CUBIC/BBR).\n     |\n  (7) TLS 1.3 HANDSHAKE                                       --> see 06-TLS\n      verify cert chain, derive keys, 1-RTT to secure channel.\n     |\n  (8) LOAD BALANCER / CDN may answer instead of origin        --> see 08-LB-CDN\n      anycast routes you to the nearest edge POP.\n     |\n  (9) DATACENTER FABRIC delivers to the actual server         --> see 09-DATACENTER\n      leaf-spine + VXLAN overlay inside the provider.\n     |\n  HTTP RESPONSE flows back up every layer, in reverse.\n```"
    },
